### Topic 48 - Spring Security with Database Users and Roles
### VS Code "REST Client" extension. Start the app first: mvn spring-boot:run
### Seeded users: admin / admin123 (ADMIN, USER)   alice / alice123 (USER)

@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Register a new user (public) -> 201
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "password": "bob12345"
}

### 2. Register the same username again -> 409 Conflict
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "bob",
  "password": "bob12345"
}

### 3. Invalid registration (short password) -> 400
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "x",
  "password": "123"
}

### 4. Who am I? (@AuthenticationPrincipal) -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/me
Authorization: Basic bob bob12345

### 5. Who am I? (SecurityContextHolder) -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/me/context
Authorization: Basic admin admin123

### 6. Create a note as alice -> 201
POST {{host}}/api/notes
Authorization: Basic alice alice123
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Groceries",
  "content": "Milk, eggs, bread"
}

### 7. alice reads HER notes -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/users/alice/notes
Authorization: Basic alice alice123

### 8. alice tries to read admin's notes -> 403 (@PreAuthorize owner check)
GET {{host}}/api/users/admin/notes
Authorization: Basic alice alice123

### 9. admin reads alice's notes -> 200 (hasRole('ADMIN'))
GET {{host}}/api/users/alice/notes
Authorization: Basic admin admin123

### 10. Admin URL as USER -> 403
GET {{host}}/api/admin/users
Authorization: Basic alice alice123

### 11. Admin URL as ADMIN -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/admin/users
Authorization: Basic admin admin123

### 12. Permission-based URL (hasAuthority('REPORT_READ')) as ADMIN -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/reports/summary
Authorization: Basic admin admin123

### 13. Delete user 3 (bob) as ADMIN -> 204
DELETE {{host}}/api/admin/users/3
Authorization: Basic admin admin123
